  "jaenFields": {
    "IMA:MdxField": {
      "documentation": {
        "value": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "depth": 1,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "U Gate",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 1,
                      "column": 3,
                      "offset": 2
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 1,
                      "column": 9,
                      "offset": 8
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 1,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 0
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 1,
                  "column": 9,
                  "offset": 8
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "In Quantum Computing, U Gate is the most important and the most fundamental single Qubit Quantum gate. All single Qubit unitary Quantum gates can be considered as a special case of the U Gate. In this chapter of the OpenQASM Tutorial, you will be learning about how to apply U Gate on a Qubit.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 3,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 10
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 3,
                      "column": 294,
                      "offset": 303
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 3,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 10
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 3,
                  "column": 294,
                  "offset": 303
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "In OpenQASM, U Gate is a built-in gate and therefore OpenQASM provides the syntax to apply U Gate on a Qubit. A U Gate has 3 parameters- θ, φ, and λ.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 5,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 305
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 5,
                      "column": 150,
                      "offset": 454
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 5,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 305
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 5,
                  "column": 150,
                  "offset": 454
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "A U Gate with parameters θ, φ, and λ can be considered as equivalent to the following operations- RZ(φ) RY(θ) RZ(λ)",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 7,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 456
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 7,
                      "column": 116,
                      "offset": 571
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 7,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 456
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 7,
                  "column": 116,
                  "offset": 571
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "where RZ(x) is rotation about the Z-axis on bloch sphere by x radians and RY(x) is rotation about the Y-axis on the bloch sphere by x radians.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 9,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 573
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 9,
                      "column": 143,
                      "offset": 715
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 9,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 573
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 9,
                  "column": 143,
                  "offset": 715
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "The U Gate with parameters θ, φ, and λ can be represented by the following matrix-",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 11,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 717
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 11,
                      "column": 83,
                      "offset": 799
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 11,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 717
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 11,
                  "column": 83,
                  "offset": 799
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "mdxJsxFlowElement",
              "name": "center",
              "attributes": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "meta": null,
                  "value": "U(\\theta,\\phi,\\lambda) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n\\cos(\\theta/2) & -e^{-i\\lambda} \\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\\ne^{i\\phi} \\sin(\\theta/2) & e^{i(\\theta+\\delta)} \\cos(\\theta/2)\n\\end{pmatrix}",
                  "data": {
                    "hName": "pre",
                    "hChildren": [
                      {
                        "type": "element",
                        "tagName": "code",
                        "properties": {
                          "className": [
                            "language-math",
                            "math-display"
                          ]
                        },
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "value": "U(\\theta,\\phi,\\lambda) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n\\cos(\\theta/2) & -e^{-i\\lambda} \\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\\ne^{i\\phi} \\sin(\\theta/2) & e^{i(\\theta+\\delta)} \\cos(\\theta/2)\n\\end{pmatrix}"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 13,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 809
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 18,
                      "column": 3,
                      "offset": 981
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 12,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 800
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 19,
                  "column": 10,
                  "offset": 991
                }
              },
              "data": {
                "_mdxExplicitJsx": true
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "For example, H Gate is a special case of U Gate when the value of θ = π/2, φ = 0 , λ = π.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 21,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 993
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 21,
                      "column": 90,
                      "offset": 1082
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 21,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 993
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 21,
                  "column": 90,
                  "offset": 1082
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "The value of parameters θ, φ, and λ can range between 0(included) and 4π(excluded).",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 23,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 1084
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 23,
                      "column": 84,
                      "offset": 1167
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 23,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1084
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 23,
                  "column": 84,
                  "offset": 1167
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "depth": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "U Gate",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 25,
                      "column": 4,
                      "offset": 1172
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 25,
                      "column": 10,
                      "offset": 1178
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 25,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1169
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 25,
                  "column": 10,
                  "offset": 1178
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "The U Gate can be applied on any Qubit.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 27,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 1180
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 27,
                      "column": 40,
                      "offset": 1219
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 27,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1180
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 27,
                  "column": 40,
                  "offset": 1219
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "The following syntax is used for applying the U Gate with parameters theta, phi, lambda on Qubit quantum_register[index]–",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 29,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 1221
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 29,
                      "column": 124,
                      "offset": 1344
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 29,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1221
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 29,
                  "column": 124,
                  "offset": 1344
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "U(theta, phi, lambda) quantum_register[index];\n",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 31,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 1346
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 32,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 1395
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "strong",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "value": "Note:",
                      "position": {
                        "start": {
                          "line": 32,
                          "column": 3,
                          "offset": 1397
                        },
                        "end": {
                          "line": 32,
                          "column": 8,
                          "offset": 1402
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 32,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 1395
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 32,
                      "column": 10,
                      "offset": 1404
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": " U is a built-in gate therefore u is a reserved keyword.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 32,
                      "column": 10,
                      "offset": 1404
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 32,
                      "column": 66,
                      "offset": 1460
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 31,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1346
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 32,
                  "column": 66,
                  "offset": 1460
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "depth": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Example",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 34,
                      "column": 5,
                      "offset": 1466
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 34,
                      "column": 12,
                      "offset": 1473
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 34,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1462
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 34,
                  "column": 12,
                  "offset": 1473
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Below is an example of applying the U Gate on first Qubit of Quantum Register qubits with parameters θ = π/2, φ = 0 , λ = π. Applying U Gate with these parameters is the equivalent of applying H Gate on the Qubit.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 36,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 1475
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 36,
                      "column": 214,
                      "offset": 1688
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 36,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1475
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 36,
                  "column": 214,
                  "offset": 1688
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "qasm",
              "meta": "playground",
              "value": "OPENQASM 2.0;\ninclude \"qelib1.inc\";\n\n// Define quantum registers\nqreg qubits[1];\n\n// Applying H gate on the first Qubit of Quantum Register\nu(pi/2, 0, pi) qubits[0];",
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 38,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1690
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 47,
                  "column": 4,
                  "offset": 1878
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "depth": 2,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "U Gate on Quantum Registers",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 49,
                      "column": 4,
                      "offset": 1883
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 49,
                      "column": 31,
                      "offset": 1910
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 49,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1880
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 49,
                  "column": 31,
                  "offset": 1910
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "It is also possible to apply U Gate with a particular set of parameters on all Qubits of a Quantum Register at once.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 51,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 1912
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 51,
                      "column": 117,
                      "offset": 2028
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 51,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 1912
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 51,
                  "column": 117,
                  "offset": 2028
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "The following syntax is used for applying the U Gate with parameters theta, phi, lambda on all Qubits of a Quantum Register quantum_register at once.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 53,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 2030
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 53,
                      "column": 151,
                      "offset": 2180
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 53,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 2030
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 53,
                  "column": 151,
                  "offset": 2180
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "qasm",
              "meta": null,
              "value": "u(theta, phi, lambda) quantum_register;",
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 55,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 2182
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 57,
                  "column": 4,
                  "offset": 2233
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "depth": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Example",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 59,
                      "column": 5,
                      "offset": 2239
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 59,
                      "column": 12,
                      "offset": 2246
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 59,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 2235
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 59,
                  "column": 12,
                  "offset": 2246
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "Below is an example of applying the U Gate on all the Qubits of Quantum Register qubits with parameters θ = π/2, φ = 0 , λ = π. Effectively, we are applying H Gate on all Qubits of the Quantum Register qubits.",
                  "position": {
                    "start": {
                      "line": 61,
                      "column": 1,
                      "offset": 2248
                    },
                    "end": {
                      "line": 61,
                      "column": 210,
                      "offset": 2457
                    }
                  }
                }
              ],
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 61,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 2248
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 61,
                  "column": 210,
                  "offset": 2457
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "qasm",
              "meta": null,
              "value": "// Applying H gate on all Qubits of the Quantum Register\nu(pi/2, 0, pi) qubits;",
              "position": {
                "start": {
                  "line": 63,
                  "column": 1,
                  "offset": 2459
                },
                "end": {
                  "line": 66,
                  "column": 4,
                  "offset": 2550
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "position": {
